{"type":"text","timestamp":1794344610407,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c745ea50001CNsiP2YYKfGfkl","messageID":"msg_1c745dfef0012E3v2NxXxrjcLK","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait — there's an issue with `from auth import bearer_token` inside the logout function — it's a local import; better to import at the top. Let me fix that.\n\nAlso `serve_frontend(request.path.lstrip(\"/\"))` in the error handler: `request.path` for \"/\" → \"\" → `os.path.join(DIST, \"\")` = DIST + \"/\" → isfile false → serves index.html. Good.\n\nAlso potential issue: `send_from_directory(DIST, path)` where path might contain \"..\" — Flask's send_from_directory protects against traversal (it uses safe_join). Good.\n\nLet me fix the bearer_token import.\n\nAlso, `int_arg(\"page_size\", ...)` — if someone passes page_size=0 → max(1, 0) = 1. Good.\n\nNow let me test the backend quickly.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794344610384,"end":1794344610403}}}
