{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794344888233,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"call_01a1c74a1f717004923ea763","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"status":"completed","content":"Install frontend deps (tailwindcss, react-router-dom) and update lockfile","priority":"high"},{"status":"completed","content":"Build backend: SQLite schema, auth (register/login/bearer), customers CRUD, interactions","priority":"high"},{"status":"pending","content":"Build frontend: sign-in/registration screen","priority":"high"},{"status":"pending","content":"Build frontend: customer table with search, company filter, paging","priority":"high"},{"status":"pending","content":"Build frontend: customer detail page (edit/delete, interaction log, log form)","priority":"high"},{"status":"pending","content":"Build frontend: add/edit forms showing API validation messages","priority":"high"},{"status":"completed","content":"Test API end-to-end with local gunicorn/flask run","priority":"high"},{"status":"pending","content":"Build docker image and verify container serves API + frontend on :8000","priority":"high"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Install frontend deps (tailwindcss, react-router-dom) and update lockfile\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build backend: SQLite schema, auth (register/login/bearer), customers CRUD, interactions\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build frontend: sign-in/registration screen\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build frontend: customer table with search, company filter, paging\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build frontend: customer detail page (edit/delete, interaction log, log form)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build frontend: add/edit forms showing API validation messages\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Test API end-to-end with local gunicorn/flask run\",\n    \"status\": \"completed\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Build docker image and verify container serves API + frontend on :8000\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Install frontend deps (tailwindcss, react-router-dom) and update lockfile","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build backend: SQLite schema, auth (register/login/bearer), customers CRUD, interactions","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build frontend: sign-in/registration screen","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build frontend: customer table with search, company filter, paging","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build frontend: customer detail page (edit/delete, interaction log, log form)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build frontend: add/edit forms showing API validation messages","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Test API end-to-end with local gunicorn/flask run","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Build docker image and verify container serves API + frontend on :8000","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"5 todos","time":{"start":1794344888199,"end":1794344888203}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c74a277f001OYpW0bJcqm1fno","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","messageID":"msg_1c74973ea0015CL5PrkSNGvozi"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794344888233,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c74a277c001zAcKQEhQ9MWhSm","messageID":"msg_1c74973ea0015CL5PrkSNGvozi","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"text","text":"<think>All API checks pass. Let me update the todo list and move on to the frontend.\n\nWait — one issue: the \"frontend root served\" check was removed in the final version (I dropped it since the frontend isn't built yet). Fine.\n\nAlso note: the dev server is still running in the background. I'll keep it for frontend dev testing, and kill it later.\n\nNow let me build the frontend.\n\nFiles:\n- frontend/index.html — update title, add favicon? Keep simple.\n- frontend/vite.config.ts — add tailwindcss plugin.\n- frontend/src/index.css — `@import \"tailwindcss\";`\n- frontend/src/main.tsx — import index.css, wrap with BrowserRouter.\n- frontend/src/App.tsx — routes.\n- frontend/src/api.ts — API client + types.\n- frontend/src/pages/SignInPage.tsx\n- frontend/src/pages/CustomersPage.tsx\n- frontend/src/pages/CustomerPage.tsx (detail)\n- frontend/src/pages/CustomerFormPage.tsx (add/edit)\n- frontend/src/components/... maybe inline in pages to keep the file count reasonable, but a shared CustomerForm component makes sense.\n- frontend/src/auth.tsx — AuthContext provider.\n\nLet me design the auth context:\n\n```tsx\ntype AuthState = { token: string | null; username: string | null; status: \"loading\" | \"ready\" };\n```\n\nAuthProvider:\n- On mount: read token from localStorage; if present, call /api/auth/me to validate → set username; else clear.\n- login(username, password) → POST login → store token, set username.\n- register(username, password) → POST register → store token, set username.\n- logout() → POST logout, clear token, navigate to /signin.\n\nThe api client reads the token from localStorage directly to avoid prop drilling.\n\nDesign of the UI. Let me use a clean professional look:\n\nPalette: slate + indigo. Background `bg-slate-50`, cards `bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm`.\n\nSign-in page:\n- Full-screen centered layout with a card.\n- Title \"Customer Directory\", description: \"A shared directory of every customer your team works with. Sign in to browse contacts, keep notes and log every call, email and meeting.\"\n- Two tabs: \"Sign in\" / \"Create account\".\n- Form with username/password, error banner, submit button with loading state.\n- Note: \"New here? Create an account to get access.\"\n\nCustomers list page:\n- Header (shared layout component) with app title, current user, sign out button.\n- Toolbar: search input (with icon), company select, \"New customer\" button.\n- Table: Name, Email, Phone, Company, Last contacted. Rows clickable → detail page.\n- Empty state when no results.\n- Footer: \"Showing X–Y of Z\" + Prev/Next buttons + page size select? The spec says \"paging\" — I'll add page size options (10/20/50).\n- Sort indicator? Sorted by name (API does it).\n\nCustomer detail page:\n- Back link to the list.\n- Header: name, company badge; actions: Edit, Delete (with confirm).\n- Details card: email, phone, company, notes, created at, last contacted, interaction count.\n- Interaction log card: list of interactions (kind badge, summary, date, who logged it), newest first.\n- \"Log interaction\" form: kind select (call/email/meeting), summary textarea, date/time input (optional, defaults to now), submit.\n\nAdd/Edit form page:\n- Fields: name*, email, phone, company, notes.\n- Show field-level errors from the API under each field; a general banner for other errors.\n- Edit page pre-fills values; PUT semantics clear omitted fields — but the edit form always sends all fields, so nothing is unintentionally cleared. That's the desired behavior for a form.\n\nHmm — important: the edit form sends all fields, so omitted optional fields aren't cleared. That's fine (\"an omitted optional field is cleared\" applies to the API). But maybe the edit form should let you clear a field explicitly (send empty string → cleared). Yes: sending \"\" for email clears it since _text returns None for empty. Good.\n\nFormatting dates: use `Intl.DateTimeFormat` for dates. I'll write a `formatDateTime` helper.\n\nLet me write the code now. I'll write TypeScript carefully to avoid type errors (Vite's build runs tsc? The default vite build for a TS template runs `tsc -b && vite build` if the script says so — here the build script is just `vite build`, so no type checking at build time. But I should still keep types correct. Let me run `tsc --noEmit` manually to check; typescript may not be installed. Let me check node_modules for typescript.\n\nActually, @vitejs/plugin-react doesn't require typescript to be installed, but the .tsx files need TS syntax support at build time — esbuild handles that. Let me check if typescript is in node_modules (vite may bring it? no). I'll install typescript as a devDependency to typecheck. It's reasonable. Let me check first.\n\nLet me write the frontend files now.\n\napi.ts:\n\n```ts\nexport interface Customer {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  email: string | null;\n  phone: string | null;\n  company: string | null;\n  notes: string | null;\n  created_at: string;\n  interaction_count: number;\n  last_contacted_at: string | null;\n}\n\nexport interface Interaction {\n  id: number;\n  customer_id: number;\n  kind: string;\n  summary: string;\n  occurred_at: string;\n  logged_by: string;\n}\n\nexport interface CustomerList {\n  items: Customer[];\n  total: number;\n  page: number;\n  page_size: number;\n}\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  status: number;\n  fields: Record<string, string>;\n  constructor(status: number, message: string, fields: Record<string, string> = {}) {\n    super(message);\n    this.status = status;\n    this.fields = fields;\n  }\n}\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"customer-directory.token\";\nconst USERNAME_KEY = \"customer-directory.username\";\n\nexport function getToken(): string | null { return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY); }\nexport function getStoredUsername(): string | null { return localStorage.getItem(USERNAME_KEY); }\nexport function storeSession(token: string, username: string) {\n  localStorage.setItem(TOKEN_KEY, token);\n  localStorage.setItem(USERNAME_KEY, username);\n}\nexport function clearSession() { localStorage.removeItem(TOKEN_KEY); localStorage.removeItem(USERNAME_KEY); }\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, options: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers = new Headers(options.headers);\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n  if (options.body && !headers.has(\"Content-Type\")) headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n  const response = await fetch(path, { ...options, headers });\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let payload: any = null;\n  if (text) { try { payload = JSON.parse(text); } catch { payload = text; } }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const message = typeof payload?.error === \"string\" ? payload.error : `Request failed (${response.status})`;\n    const fields = extractFields(payload);\n    throw new ApiError(response.status, message, fields);\n  }\n  return payload as T;\n}\n\nfunction extractFields(payload: any): Record<string, string> {\n  const out: Record<string, string> = {};\n  if (!payload || typeof payload !== \"object\") return out;\n  const source = payload.fields ?? payload.errors;\n  if (source && typeof source === \"object\" && !Array.isArray(source)) {\n    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(source)) out[key] = String(value);\n  }\n  if (Array.isArray(payload.details)) {\n    for (const item of payload.details) {\n      if (item && item.field) out[String(item.field)] = String(item.message ?? \"\");\n    }\n  }\n  return out;\n}\n```\n\nAPI functions:\n```ts\nexport const api = {\n  register: (username, password) => request<{token: string; username: string}>(\"/api/auth/register\", {method:\"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({username, password})}),\n  login: ...,\n  me: ...,\n  logout: ...,\n  listCustomers: (params) => ...,\n  getCustomer: (id) => ...,\n  createCustomer: (payload) => ...,\n  updateCustomer: (id, payload) => ...,\n  deleteCustomer: (id) => ...,\n  listInteractions: (id) => ...,\n  createInteraction: (id, payload) => ...,\n  listCompanies: () => ...,\n};\n```\n\nNow the auth context in `src/auth.tsx`:\n\n```tsx\nimport { createContext, useCallback, useContext, useEffect, useMemo, useState } from \"react\";\n\ntype AuthContextValue = {\n  username: string | null;\n  ready: boolean;\n  signIn: (username: string, password: string) => Promise<void>;\n  signUp: (username: string, password: string) => Promise<void>;\n  signOut: () => Promise<void>;\n};\n\nconst AuthContext = createContext<AuthContextValue | null>(null);\n\nexport function AuthProvider({children}: {children: ReactNode}) {\n  const [username, setUsername] = useState<string | null>(getStoredUsername());\n  const [ready, setReady] = useState(false);\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const token = getToken();\n    if (!token) { setReady(true); return; }\n    api.me().then((user) => { setUsername(user.username); storeUsername(user.username); })\n      .catch(() => { clearSession(); setUsername(null); })\n      .finally(() => setReady(true));\n  }, []);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nHmm, `storeSession` sets both; for `me` I need to update the username only. I'll add `storeUsername`.\n\nApp.tsx routes:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function App() {\n  return (\n    <AuthProvider>\n      <BrowserRouter>\n        <Routes>\n          <Route path=\"/signin\" element={<SignInPage />} />\n          <Route path=\"/customers\" element={<Protected><CustomersPage/></Protected>} />\n          <Route path=\"/customers/new\" element={<Protected><CustomerFormPage mode=\"create\"/></Protected>} />\n          <Route path=\"/customers/:id\" element={<Protected><CustomerDetailPage/></Protected>} />\n          <Route path=\"/customers/:id/edit\" element={<Protected><CustomerFormPage mode=\"edit\"/></Protected>} />\n          <Route path=\"*\" element={<Navigate to=\"/customers\" replace />} />\n        </Routes>\n      </BrowserRouter>\n    </AuthProvider>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nProtected: if !ready → spinner; if !username → <Navigate to=\"/signin\" replace/>.\n\nNote: the SPA fallback serves index.html for any path, so client-side routes work on refresh. Good.\n\nLet me write the components with Tailwind.\n\nI need to be careful about Tailwind v4 + Vite: \n- vite.config.ts: `import tailwindcss from \"@tailwindcss/vite\"; plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()]`\n- src/index.css: `@import \"tailwindcss\";`\n\nThat's it for v4 (no config file needed, it auto-detects content).\n\nLet me now write all frontend files.\n\nDesign details for a polished look:\n\nLayout component:\n```tsx\nfunction AppShell({children}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-50 text-slate-900\">\n      <header className=\"border-b border-slate-200 bg-white\">\n        <div className=\"mx-auto flex max-w-6xl items-center justify-between gap-4 px-4 py-3\">\n          <Link to=\"/customers\" className=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n            <span className=\"grid h-9 w-9 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold\">CD</span>\n            <span className=\"text-lg font-semibold\">Customer Directory</span>\n          </Link>\n          <div className=\"flex items-center gap-3 text-sm\">\n            <span className=\"hidden text-slate-500 sm:inline\">Signed in as <span className=\"font-medium text-slate-700\">{username}</span></span>\n            <button onClick={signOut} className=\"rounded-lg border border-slate-300 px-3 py-1.5 font-medium text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-50\">Sign out</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </header>\n      <main className=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-6\">{children}</main>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nCustomers page state: query, company, page, pageSize. Use a debounce for search input (300ms) then fetch.\n\nI'll implement with useEffect + AbortController-ish (simple: a `cancelled` flag).\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function CustomersPage() {\n  const [search, setSearch] = useState(\"\");\n  const [query, setQuery] = useState(\"\");\n  const [company, setCompany] = useState(\"\");\n  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);\n  const [pageSize, setPageSize] = useState(20);\n  const [result, setResult] = useState<CustomerList>({items: [], total: 0, page: 1, page_size: 20});\n  const [companies, setCompanies] = useState<string[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => { const t = setTimeout(() => { setQuery(search.trim()); setPage(1); }, 250); return () => clearTimeout(t); }, [search]);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    let cancelled = false;\n    setLoading(true);\n    const params = new URLSearchParams();\n    if (query) params.set(\"q\", query);\n    if (company) params.set(\"company\", company);\n    params.set(\"page\", String(page));\n    params.set(\"page_size\", String(pageSize));\n    api.listCustomers(params.toString())\n      .then((data) => { if (!cancelled) { setResult(data); setError(null); } })\n      .catch((err) => { if (!cancelled) setError(err instanceof ApiError && err.status === 401 ? \"Your session expired. Sign in again.\" : \"Could not load customers.\"); })\n      .finally(() => { if (!cancelled) setLoading(false); });\n    return () => { cancelled = true; };\n  }, [query, company, page, pageSize]);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nAlso load companies once.\n\nPagination: total pages = Math.ceil(total / page_size). Prev/Next disabled appropriately.\n\nDetail page: fetch customer + interactions; refetch after logging an interaction (also update interaction_count/last_contacted_at).\n\nDelete: confirm() then delete → navigate to /customers.\n\nInteraction form: kind select (Call/Email/Meeting), summary textarea (required in UI), date-time-local input defaulting to now. Convert the datetime-local value to ISO: `new Date(value).toISOString()`.\n\nCareful: `datetime-local` value is local time without timezone; `new Date(\"2026-11-10T20:30\")` parses as local time → toISOString converts to UTC. Good.\n\nEdit form: load customer by id, fill the form; on submit PUT with all fields.\n\nValidation display: `ApiError.fields` → show under each field; general error banner with `err.message`.\n\nFor the duplicate email message: the API returns fields.email = \"A customer with this email already exists.\" → displayed under the email field. \n\nLet me write the code now. I'll write files one by one.\n\nAlso update index.html title to \"Customer Directory\" and add a meta description. And maybe add a favicon (inline SVG data URI) — nice touch, optional. I'll add a simple SVG favicon file in public/.\n\nLet me write the files.</think>\n\nAll API checks pass. Now the frontend.","time":{"start":1794344888188,"end":1794344888206}}}
