{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794345016849,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c74c1df900119cdsJydb9oXOK","messageID":"msg_1c74c0b32001IinYpilCzyvpOr","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794345016849,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c74c1dfc001Awerixd81YRYJ9","messageID":"msg_1c74c0b32001IinYpilCzyvpOr","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"text","text":"<think>Tailwind utilities are generated. TypeScript is not installed. Let me install it as a devDependency to typecheck the code (good practice, and the tsconfig needs to exist too — there's no tsconfig.json in the project! Vite's react plugin handles TSX without tsconfig, but for editor support and typechecking, a tsconfig is needed).\n\nThe starter project has no tsconfig.json. Let me add one (standard Vite React TS template) and install typescript + @types/react + @types/react-dom for typechecking. That improves quality. The Docker build only runs `npm run build` (vite build), which doesn't typecheck — but I want to verify types are correct myself.\n\nAdding typescript to devDependencies means the Docker build installs it too (npm ci). It's a dev dependency; the frontend build stage installs dev deps by default. That adds install time but is fine.\n\nHmm, is there a risk? `npm ci` requires package-lock.json to be in sync with package.json. I'll run `npm install` to update the lock file.\n\nLet me install typescript and the @types packages.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794345016828,"end":1794345016844}}}
