{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794345039947,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c74c7834001gqwH5KqCqfKyzW","messageID":"msg_1c74c547d001MEYm77hjLZi8WO","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794345039947,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"id":"prt_1c74c7837001uC0ZrMjkbKnACd","messageID":"msg_1c74c547d001MEYm77hjLZi8WO","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","type":"text","text":"<think>Type checking passes. Note `vite.config.ts` is included but uses `defineConfig` — fine.\n\nWait, `noUnusedLocals` is on and it passed. Good.\n\nNow let me add a `typecheck` script to package.json and maybe a `lint`? No lint configured. Let me add \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\" to package.json scripts — useful and harmless.\n\nLet me update package.json scripts:\n```json\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"dev\": \"vite\",\n  \"build\": \"vite build\",\n  \"typecheck\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n  \"preview\": \"vite preview\"\n}\n```\n\nHmm, \"build\" should maybe run typecheck too: \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit && vite build\". That would make the Docker build fail on type errors — risky but good practice. If typescript isn't installed in the Docker build (it is, devDeps are installed by npm ci), it works. But it slows the build slightly. I'll keep build as just \"vite build\" to avoid a build-breaking typecheck, and add a separate \"typecheck\" script. Actually, having the build catch type errors is valuable... but the risk of a failing Docker build outweighs it. Keep them separate.\n\nNow let me test the frontend in a browser-ish way. I can't run a browser, but I can:\n1. Build and serve the dist from the Flask app (the backend serves frontend/dist).\n2. Check that the SPA routes return index.html.\n3. Verify the API works with the built frontend.\n\nI should also do a smoke test of the React app rendering. Without a browser, I can't fully verify. Let me check if a headless browser is available (puppeteer/playwright?) — unlikely in the sandbox, but let me check for chromium.\n\nActually, I can do a server-side render smoke test using react-dom/server to render App to a string — but App uses BrowserRouter which requires window/history. I could use StaticRouter (react-router-dom/server) to render the SignIn page and check for errors. That would catch runtime errors in the component code (e.g., undefined imports). Let me do that with a small node script using tsx? I don't have tsx installed. I could use vite's SSR build or esbuild.\n\nSimpler: use `vite build --ssr` on a small entry that renders the app to a string. Let me try:\n\nCreate `frontend/src/ssr-check.tsx`:\n```tsx\nimport { renderToString } from \"react-dom/server\";\nimport { StaticRouter } from \"react-router-dom/server\";\nimport App from \"./App\";\nconsole.log(renderToString(<StaticRouter location=\"/signin\"><App/></StaticRouter>));\n```\nBut App includes AuthProvider which calls localStorage in useEffect (not run during SSR) and `getStoredUsername()` in useState initializer → calls window.localStorage → ReferenceError in Node. I'd need to guard. I could stub globalThis.window in the SSR check script.\n\nLet me instead do a jsdom-based test? jsdom isn't installed.\n\nAlternative: check if playwright/chromium exists in the sandbox for a real browser test.\n\nLet me check quickly: `which chromium chromium-browser google-chrome; ls /root/.cache/ms-playwright`.\n\nLet me check.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794345039927,"end":1794345039943}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794345040700,"sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c74c74457011ab7bd869","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"which chromium chromium-browser google-chrome google-chrome-stable 2>/dev/null; ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright 2>/dev/null; python3 -c \"import playwright\" 2>&1 | tail -1; npm ls -g --depth=0 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'playwright'\n/usr/local/lib\n├── corepack@0.36.0\n├── npm@11.19.1\n└── opencode-ai@1.18.35\n\n","metadata":{"output":"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'playwright'\n/usr/local/lib\n├── corepack@0.36.0\n├── npm@11.19.1\n└── opencode-ai@1.18.35\n\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"which chromium chromium-browser google-chrome google-chrome-stable 2>/dev/null; ls ~/.cache/ms-playwright 2>/dev/null; python3 -c \"import playwright\" 2>&1 | tail -1; npm ls -g --depth=0 2>/dev/null | head -20","time":{"start":1794345039935,"end":1794345040682}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c74c7839001IbyMhRuKPg8uxk","sessionID":"ses_e38be2834ffeyfE9hooqtrOekt","messageID":"msg_1c74c547d001MEYm77hjLZi8WO"}}
